WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.635 --> 00:00:04.536
Take a break!

00:00:05.907 --> 00:00:07.980
If you find yourself stuck on something

00:00:08.155 --> 00:00:10.447
if you find yourself unable to make progress

00:00:10.739 --> 00:00:11.999
on a project that you’re working on

00:00:12.562 --> 00:00:13.625
take a break.

00:00:14.595 --> 00:00:16.856
Because often if you’re just trying to ram something through

00:00:17.082 --> 00:00:19.052
you’re not going to get the results that you’re looking for

00:00:19.311 --> 00:00:20.809
and if you take 10 minutes

00:00:21.475 --> 00:00:23.571
go away from it and come back

00:00:24.655 --> 00:00:25.665
you’ll often be refreshed

00:00:25.665 --> 00:00:27.235
and be able to solve the problem.

00:00:27.765 --> 00:00:30.356
Two quick stories for you that happened to me recently

00:00:30.356 --> 00:00:34.753
so yesterday Jason who was helping me with my new website

00:00:34.954 --> 00:00:36.391
and all the branding that goes with it

00:00:36.922 --> 00:00:38.327
he’s working on some coding problem

00:00:38.652 --> 00:00:39.495
something on the website

00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:41.463
some bug that he’s trying to work through

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.017
and he couldn’t find a solution.

00:00:43.161 --> 00:00:44.809
And he’s spending like an hour on this thing

00:00:45.016 --> 00:00:47.439
and I just see him on the computer like

00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:48.971
“Ugh”, rubbing his eyes

00:00:49.262 --> 00:00:51.668
and unable to make progress on this thing.

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:54.395
And so he does a smart thing

00:00:54.588 --> 00:00:55.511
and he goes and he takes a break.

00:00:56.427 --> 00:00:57.479
He goes out, goes for a walk

00:00:57.707 --> 00:00:59.093
get some food, comes back

00:00:59.304 --> 00:01:01.967
and within 5 minutes of sitting down again he solves it.

00:01:02.658 --> 00:01:04.823
And this happens to me so much

00:01:05.551 --> 00:01:07.487
and I don’t know what it is about the human condition

00:01:07.708 --> 00:01:11.180
that allows us to do this

00:01:11.539 --> 00:01:15.413
but I often find myself with these kinds of problems

00:01:15.707 --> 00:01:17.775
and I may come back with the next day

00:01:17.933 --> 00:01:18.839
or maybe it’s the next day

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.085
but the solution often comes really quickly

00:01:21.085 --> 00:01:22.510
after taking a break.

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:24.897
So again, if you’re finding yourself pounding away with something

00:01:24.897 --> 00:01:26.397
and you’re just not making progress

00:01:26.639 --> 00:01:28.203
you just can’t figure out what the problem is

00:01:28.797 --> 00:01:31.626
take a break, even like 10, 15 minutes

00:01:31.835 --> 00:01:32.595
and come back to it.

00:01:33.081 --> 00:01:35.981
Another quick example is in salsa dancing.

00:01:36.713 --> 00:01:37.504
I love salsa dancing,

00:01:37.678 --> 00:01:39.535
I love teaching people how to dance as well

00:01:39.763 --> 00:01:41.459
and I was working with a student

00:01:42.025 --> 00:01:44.522
teaching her how to do some turns

00:01:45.624 --> 00:01:47.707
and she just wasn’t getting it.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.648
And so I said, “Okay you know what, it’s okay.

00:01:50.938 --> 00:01:51.966
It’s okay, we’ll come back to it

00:01:52.103 --> 00:01:52.874
we’ll move on to other stuff.”

00:01:53.405 --> 00:01:54.975
And it was an hour that I was with her

00:01:56.104 --> 00:01:56.957
and we did other moves

00:01:57.187 --> 00:01:58.687
and at the end of the hour we came back

00:01:58.914 --> 00:02:01.047
and we did the turn again and she got it.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.599
And so the first example was programming, business related.

00:02:05.776 --> 00:02:08.648
This was salsa dancing, personal, a new skill.

00:02:08.986 --> 00:02:10.347
Anytime you’re trying to figure something out

00:02:10.515 --> 00:02:13.298
if you’re doing it over and over and over again

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.898
and it’s just not working out for whatever reason

00:02:16.096 --> 00:02:17.455
I don’t know why this happens

00:02:19.375 --> 00:02:21.454
but if you’re not making progress, stop

00:02:22.604 --> 00:02:24.135
and come back to it later that day

00:02:24.375 --> 00:02:25.136
or the next day

00:02:25.326 --> 00:02:28.586
and you’ll amaze yourself with how you’re able to quickly make progress

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.486
and think “Why didn’t I think of that before?”

00:02:32.974 --> 00:02:33.945
So take a break.

00:02:34.411 --> 00:02:35.399
Believe.

